InfinityGrid Headline
STRYKER: WHEN THE DEFENSIVE CONTROL PLANE BECAME THE DESTRUCTIVE WEAPON

And underneath:

No ransomware needed. No confirmed zero-day required. Enterprise management authority itself became the blast radius.

That is the angle that takes this well beyond “Stryker suffered a cyberattack.” It turns the case into an enterprise architecture lesson about identity, administrative trust, RBAC, privileged access, Intune, destructive action controls, monitoring, and resilience—while still staying disciplined about what Stryker actually confirmed versus what Handala and outside researchers claimed.
